WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.877 --> 00:00:15.607
When Heidi woke up the next morning, at first she could not remember where she was.

2
00:00:16.207 --> 00:00:21.131
Then she heard Grandfather's deep voice coming from the room below and she climbed down the ladder.

3
00:00:21.812 --> 00:00:24.274
While they were having breakfast, they heard a loud whistle.

4
00:00:25.435 --> 00:00:28.557
They went outside, and there stood Peter with his herd of goats.

5
00:00:28.577 --> 00:00:31.520
"Do you want to go with them up the mountain?"

6
00:00:31.952 --> 00:00:32.913
asked Grandfather.

7
00:00:33.293 --> 00:00:34.935
Nothing could have pleased Heidi more.

8
00:00:37.457 --> 00:00:40.679
She started joyfully up the mountain with Peter and the goats.

9
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:45.163
Soon, she was running here, there, and everywhere, shouting with delight.

10
00:00:46.024 --> 00:00:48.626
She was enchanted by the waving fields of flowers.

11
00:00:49.687 --> 00:00:53.870
Whenever she caught sight of a bright patch of red or yellow blossoms, she ran off.

12
00:00:54.471 --> 00:00:57.873
She picked handfuls of the fresh flowers and carried them in her apron.

13
00:00:58.434 --> 00:01:00.996
She wanted to take them all home and stick them in the hay.

14
00:01:01.632 --> 00:01:04.594
She wanted to make her bedroom look just like the mountain meadows.

15
00:01:04.615 --> 00:01:07.397
"Where are you now, Heidi?"

16
00:01:07.697 --> 00:01:08.518
Peter called out.

17
00:01:09.038 --> 00:01:09.979
Heidi looked around.

18
00:01:10.559 --> 00:01:13.341
Some of the goats had followed her, but she couldn't see Peter.

19
00:01:14.022 --> 00:01:15.643
"Here," she called back.

20
00:01:15.663 --> 00:01:17.965
"We still have a long way to go!"

21
00:01:18.385 --> 00:01:19.326
called Peter again.

22
00:01:20.627 --> 00:01:24.050
Then he whistled loudly and started calling the goats by name.

23
00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:27.513
One after the other they bounded off, and Heidi followed.

24
00:01:27.933 --> 00:01:33.101
Surrounded by the goats, Peter led the way to a green plateau, where the goats could nibble juicy

25
00:01:33.121 --> 00:01:35.182
stems while he and Heidi ate lunch.

26
00:01:36.703 --> 00:01:37.563
Heidi sat down.

27
00:01:37.583 --> 00:01:39.204
"Is the milk for me?"

28
00:01:39.444 --> 00:01:39.964
she asked.

29
00:01:39.984 --> 00:01:45.627
"Yes," replied Peter, "and the two large pieces of bread, and the cheese is yours too."

30
00:01:46.148 --> 00:01:49.790
Grandfather had packed a lunch for Heidi and given it to Peter to carry.

31
00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:52.291
It was much bigger than Peter's own lunch.

32
00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:57.174
Heidi cut off big chunks of her bread and cheese and gave them to Peter.

33
00:01:57.194 --> 00:02:01.336
"Here, you can have this, I have plenty," she said.

34
00:02:01.984 --> 00:02:05.085
Peter looked at Heidi with astonishment, unable to speak.

35
00:02:05.486 --> 00:02:07.546
Then he shyly nodded his thanks.

36
00:02:08.887 --> 00:02:12.729
All of a sudden, Peter leapt to his feet and ran after a goat that was leaping in

37
00:02:12.769 --> 00:02:14.469
the direction of some dangerous rocks.

38
00:02:14.889 --> 00:02:18.751
When he brought the goat back to where they were eating, Peter lifted his stick to hit the

39
00:02:18.791 --> 00:02:23.093
goat. "No, no, Peter, you must not hit her.

40
00:02:23.573 --> 00:02:25.034
See how frightened she is?"

41
00:02:25.594 --> 00:02:27.495
"She deserves it," growled Peter.

42
00:02:27.515 --> 00:02:30.396
"It will hurt her, leave her alone!"

43
00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:33.781
Peter looked with surprise at the outspoken little girl.

44
00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:37.962
"Well, I will let her off if you will give me some more cheese tomorrow."

45
00:02:37.982 --> 00:02:43.004
"You shall have some tomorrow and every day," Heidi agreed.

46
00:02:43.504 --> 00:02:46.685
And she made Peter promise not to hit any of the goats ever again.

47
00:02:47.265 --> 00:02:52.266
After a long afternoon, the sun began to sink behind the mountain, and the rocks began to glow

48
00:02:52.346 --> 00:02:53.947
red with the sun's fading light.

49
00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:58.348
It was a beautiful sight, and Heidi jumped to her feet.

50
00:02:58.892 --> 00:03:00.073
"Peter! Peter!"

51
00:03:00.353 --> 00:03:00.953
she cried.

52
00:03:00.973 --> 00:03:02.814
"Everything is on fire!"

53
00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:05.436
"It is always like that," said Peter.

54
00:03:05.456 --> 00:03:07.337
"It will happen again tomorrow.

55
00:03:07.697 --> 00:03:09.978
But we must go home now, it's getting late."

56
00:03:10.459 --> 00:03:12.680
Heidi had never had a better day in her life.

57
00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:17.963
She loved the beauty of the mountainside, and the sun setting behind the mountaintop.

58
00:03:18.443 --> 00:03:22.705
As Heidi arrived at her hut, Peter called out from the path, "Good night!

59
00:03:23.046 --> 00:03:24.386
Come with me again tomorrow!"

60
00:03:24.806 --> 00:03:28.964
Heidi quickly ran back and shook Peter's hand, promising to go with him again.
